# Cloudflare Pages redirects. PATH ONLY — this file cannot match on hostname,
# so the buildpays.com.au -> paykicker.com.au move is NOT here. That is a
# host-level redirect and lives as a Cloudflare rule on the zone.
#
# These are the URLs the PayKicker rename actually broke. All three were live,
# indexed by Google, and started 404ing the moment the files were renamed.

# The explainer. Iframed on the old homepage, listed in the old sitemap, and
# indexed — so it is reached by real visitors, not just crawlers.
/buildpays-explainer            /paykicker-explainer            301
/buildpays-explainer.html       /paykicker-explainer            301

# The worker training walkthrough. Linked from onboarding SMS messages ALREADY
# SENT to workers' phones — those links cannot be edited after the fact, so this
# redirect is the only thing keeping them alive.
/buildpays-worker-training      /paykicker-worker-training      301
/buildpays-worker-training.html /paykicker-worker-training      301

# Old image filenames. Social platforms and search engines cached these as the
# og:image and schema.org logo, and re-fetch them long after a rename.
/buildpays-logo.png             /paykicker-logo.png             301
/buildpays-logo-dark.png        /paykicker-logo-dark.png        301
/buildpays-icon.png             /paykicker-icon-512.png         301
